## 12. GitHub Actions Runner

The runner is the server where the pipeline executes, the repository is cloned, and (by default) the ZTP file share is hosted. `RUNNER_DEPLOYMENT_MODE` controls whether Pipeline 0 deploys a new VM or connects to an existing server.

### 12.1 Deployment Control

| Variable Name | Value | Description |
|---------------|-------|-------------|
| RUNNER_DEPLOYMENT_MODE | [CHANGE-ME] | How the runner is provisioned: `deploy_azure_vm`, `existing_azure_vm`, `existing_onprem`, `manual` |
| RUNNER_SKIP_AGENT_INSTALL | false | Skip GitHub Actions agent installation (operator handles it) |
| RUNNER_SKIP_PREREQUISITES | false | Skip prerequisite software installation (PS7, Git, Az CLI, VS Code) |

### 12.2 Server Identity

| Variable Name | Value | Description |
|---------------|-------|-------------|
| RUNNER_IP_ADDRESS | [CHANGE-ME] | Runner server IP address |
| RUNNER_HOSTNAME | [CHANGE-ME] | Windows computer name (15 character max) |
| RUNNER_FQDN | [CHANGE-ME] | Fully qualified domain name |
| RUNNER_OS | Windows Server 2025 | Operating system |
| RUNNER_DOMAIN_JOINED | true | Whether the server is/should be domain-joined |

### 12.3 GitHub Agent Configuration

| Variable Name | Value | Description |
|---------------|-------|-------------|
| RUNNER_AGENT_ORG | [CHANGE-ME] | GitHub organization |
| RUNNER_AGENT_REPO | [CHANGE-ME] | GitHub repository name |
| RUNNER_AGENT_REPO_URL | [CHANGE-ME] | Full clone URL (supports forks, GHE) |
| RUNNER_AGENT_GROUP | default | GitHub runner group |
| RUNNER_AGENT_LABELS | self-hosted, Windows, ztp | Comma-separated runner labels |
| RUNNER_AGENT_NAME | [CHANGE-ME] | Runner display name in GitHub Actions |
| RUNNER_AGENT_PAT_SECRET | github-runner-pat | Key Vault secret name for GitHub PAT |
| RUNNER_AGENT_INSTALL_DIR | C:\actions-runner | Runner agent install directory |
| RUNNER_REPO_CLONE_DIR | C:\git\[REPO_NAME] | Where the repository is cloned |

### 12.4 Share Configuration

The ZTP file share runs on the runner by default. To host the share on a different server, change `RUNNER_SHARE_SERVER_IP`.

| Variable Name | Value | Description |
|---------------|-------|-------------|
| RUNNER_SHARE_SERVER_IP | [CHANGE-ME] | Share host IP (defaults to RUNNER_IP_ADDRESS if blank) |
| RUNNER_SHARE_NAME | ztp | SMB share name |
| RUNNER_SHARE_LOCAL_PATH | C:\share\ztp | Local filesystem path for the share |
| RUNNER_SHARE_NETWORK_PATH | [AUTO] | UNC path — auto-composed from server_ip + name if blank |
| RUNNER_SHARE_ACCESS_USERNAME | svc_idrac_share | Local user created for iDRAC share access |
| RUNNER_SHARE_ACCESS_PWD_SECRET | share-access-password | Key Vault secret for share password |
| RUNNER_SHARE_SKIP_SETUP | false | Skip share creation (share already exists) |
| RUNNER_SHARE_SKIP_USER | false | Skip local user creation (user already exists) |
| RUNNER_SHARE_EXTRA_DISK | false | Use a dedicated data disk for share storage |
| RUNNER_SHARE_DISK_SIZE_GB | 256 | Data disk size in GB (when extra_disk is true) |
| RUNNER_SHARE_DISK_LETTER | D | Drive letter for the data disk |

